# APK matches the site

## Channel-first (must match web)

- Primary Asker UX is the **public Clevertree/IRC room** (default `#mp-general`), not tip-mint / SubmitTicketForm.
- APK home loads the room via WebView of `https://myproblem.app/c/mp-general` (same room as `/#room`). Type / speak / video → Bunny → `/api/chat/post` through that page — same APIs as web.
- Tickets open **only when AI/batch decides** they are needed. Do not mint tips on every ask; do not push tip-repo submit or “New ticket” as the foundation path.
- Public chat + channel AI stay free forever. Private chat fees (copy only if shown) later fund infra — no tip-push CTAs.
- Endpoints live in `ChatEndpoints.kt` and must stay aligned with `src/lib/contact.ts` + `src/lib/chat/channels.ts`.

## FixIt screens (native)

- Ticket list / detail / Networker still draw FixIt in Compose (not a full-site WebView).
- Colors and the 900px split live in `src/styles/fixit-theme.css`. The app copies are `AppColors.kt` and `SiteLayout.kt` (`DESKTOP_MIN_PX = 900`). Change both when the site tokens or breakpoint change.
- Ticket status words live in `src/lib/tickets/ticketStatus.ts` and `TicketPageStatus.kt`. An open ticket is Awaiting review. Do not mark a fix plan current.
- Phone width is one column. A window of 900px or wider uses the desktop arrangement (960 cap, two columns where the site does).
- Marketing, privacy, and terms stay on the website. Link out. Do not rebuild those pages in Compose.
- Debug-only tools (E2E receiver, Test screen, legacy tip-mint routes, Server ahead) stay out of release product chrome.
